{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"92d1bea469e6fa935cf325661ffaccc2927f2d9f9ed9f65df65f52a9fae5e948","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_92c0cce1435bb09ec0152817b62a599479b526dd086a9680abe236586752e705","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technically sound contribution to hierarchical reinforcement learning but fails to meet key policy and compliance standards for a double-blind review. The most significant issue is the explicit violation of anonymity rules through the inclusion of author names, affiliations, and emails on the title page. Additionally, the paper lacks a broader impact statement and ethical considerations, which are standard expectations for responsible AI research. Data usage is compliant as it relies on synthetic simulation environments.","paper_id":"B1oK8aoxe","paper_identity_sha256":"9975c2c80fcb1346a055ef543d7f00c30ac71d33e71f84bfcf5b1e272b1f8ccd","prompt_identity_sha256":"3a20a09e45532ce856132f604cd9115abf64cd5193d59fc09a441a09786f0ce0","raw_response_sha256":"d31633d8f352bd189a805d1d1206ba96cfd84527d9e97f06662815977caf2b6e","request_identity_sha256":"37077f022bd4caeb9d4121cb5ef23cee90378fb55b65b2872eadcd981be4c7d6","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a dedicated section on ethics, responsible AI, or potential societal harms. While the work focuses on reinforcement learning for robotic control (swimmer, ant, mazes), which generally carries lower immediate ethical risk than, for example, autonomous weapons or social media manipulation, the absence of any discussion on dual-use potential, fairness, or bias is notable. The authors do not address whether the learned skills could be misused or if the proxy reward mechanisms might inadvertently encourage unsafe behaviors in more complex, real-world robotic applications. Given the 2017 venue context, a formal ethics statement was less common, but a brief mention of safety considerations or limitations regarding deployment in sensitive environments would have strengthened the responsible AI compliance.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-024"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes standard simulation environments (e.g., MuJoCo-based tasks like Swimmer, Ant, and Maze) for its experiments. No real-world data, human subjects, or personally identifiable information (PII) are involved. The data usage is compliant with standard academic research practices for simulation-based reinforcement learning. There are no privacy violations or licensing issues associated with the synthetic data generated during the training process. The paper does not claim to use any proprietary or restricted datasets that would require specific consent or licensing disclosures.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-039"],"review_text":"The submission violates double-blind review policies. The title page explicitly lists the authors' names (Carlos Florensa, Yan Duan, Pieter Abbeel) and their institutional affiliations (UC Berkeley, OpenAI). Additionally, the email addresses (florensa@berkeley.edu, {rocky, pieter}@openai.com) are provided, which directly identify the authors. The Acknowledgments section also names specific individuals and funding sources (DARPA, BVLC, BAIR, BDD, ONR, La Caixa, Huawei) that can be used to infer author identities and institutional ties. These elements compromise the anonymity required for a fair double-blind review process.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-008","SRC-009"],"review_text":"There is no evidence of plagiarism or dual submission within the provided text. The paper cites relevant prior work appropriately, including distinct contributions from related fields such as hierarchical RL and intrinsic motivation. The methodology and experimental setup appear to be original contributions, with clear differentiation from cited works like Heess et al. (2016) and Daniel et al. (2012). The text does not contain large verbatim overlaps with other known publications, and the figures and tables are described as specific to this work's experiments.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-036","SRC-037"],"review_text":"The paper lacks a comprehensive broader impact statement or a completed responsible research checklist, which are increasingly expected in modern ML venues. While the Discussion section (Section 8) outlines technical limitations and future work, it does not explicitly address the societal implications, environmental impact of training compute, or the potential for the learned skills to be applied in harmful contexts. The paper does not mention software or data licensing terms for any released code or models. The absence of these elements represents a gap in broader impact compliance, although the technical focus on simulation reduces the immediate societal risk profile.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"bf9437721fa4e453c93ddc91ce2623a306682c43c304587b581a0769034092f4","paper_id":"B1oK8aoxe","paper_ordinal":15,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"d31633d8f352bd189a805d1d1206ba96cfd84527d9e97f06662815977caf2b6e","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1oK8aoxe","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"5782bbf1cd97a2f8bec317cf8672f220d996dcc97a19979ff10f01b41d2b98c9","request_identity_sha256":"37077f022bd4caeb9d4121cb5ef23cee90378fb55b65b2872eadcd981be4c7d6","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v2","usage":{"completion_tokens":979,"prompt_tokens":16880,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":17859},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"37077f022bd4caeb9d4121cb5ef23cee90378fb55b65b2872eadcd981be4c7d6","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v1"}